:ruby
  Heading = import("/components/Layout/Heading")
  CallbackException = import("./CallbackException")
  ErrorBoundaryExample = import("./ErrorBoundaryExample")
  UnhandledRenderException = import("./UnhandledRenderException")

%article
  %Heading(level=2) Exceptions
  %p
    Callback errors and render errors follow different paths. Callback errors
    are reported by the runtime, while render errors can be recovered by the
    nearest parent error boundary. Without a boundary, a render error reaches
    the document and is reported like a callback error.

  .examples
    %CallbackException
    %ErrorBoundaryExample
    %UnhandledRenderException

:css
  .examples {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
